## 2. User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **VRAM & Compute Considerations for 3D Convolutions**:
> Processing 16-frame video tensors `[3, 16, 224, 224]` with 3D convolutions uses significantly more GPU memory than 2D single frames.
> We recommend a **batch size of 8 or 16** with **Automatic Mixed Precision (AMP)** enabled to comfortably fit within your NVIDIA RTX 4060 GPU (8GB VRAM).

> [!NOTE]
> **3D Video Backbone Selection**:
> We will use `torchvision.models.video.r2plus1d_18(weights='KINETICS400_V1')` as the primary 3D backbone. R(2+1)D factorizes 3D convolutions into separate 2D spatial and 1D temporal convolutions, yielding superior accuracy and efficiency for action/engagement recognition.

